# Simple code

Highest-priority rule. Dense or clever `core/` / engine code is a bug. Architecture folders do not excuse it.

Do: use domain words (stroke, region, layer, dab, tool); one method, one step; early `return`; named locals; `List<DrawingStroke>` not `List<T>`; comment only the why.

Do not: mini-frameworks, pipelines, registries; mixins, `typedef`, `dynamic`, operator overloads, codegen for drawing; hide flow in callbacks when a method call would do; split a 20-line method into five 3-line helpers.

If two plain classes are clearer than one abstract one, write two.

```dart
// BAD — the chain hides the work
final ids = strokes.where((s) => s.regionId == id).map((s) => s.id).toList();

// GOOD — a reader sees the filter
final ids = <int>[];
for (final stroke in strokes) {
  if (stroke.regionId == id) {
    ids.add(stroke.id);
  }
}
```
